Solution: Continue with an isolated RendererFeature migration instead of touching massive Core files or creating new Contracts. Candidate selection is constrained to Presentation/Visor files where material scalar/vector state can be packed into a global CBuffer without gameplay truth changes.
Rejected Alternatives: Rewriting all remaining Visor features in one pass was rejected as compile-wall risk. Editing unrelated Core/World/Input files was rejected as domain breach. MaterialPropertyBlock was rejected for full-screen renderer features because the required direction is global CBuffers/GraphicsBuffers.
