## Decision 03 - Visor Post CBuffer Sweep
Problem: After the previous pass, multiple small fullscreen Presentation passes still pushed synchronized post-process constants through material mutation. VR brownout, retina distortion, stochastic SSR, and visor fluid distortion were isolated enough to migrate without touching gameplay truth or shared contracts. `HectonVisorFluidDistortionFeature` also carried a runtime `Pack=1` telemetry DTO and a concrete `PlayerRuntimeContextService` fallback.
Solution: Added four named global CBuffers: `HectonVRBrownoutGlobals` (64 bytes), `HectonRetinaDistortionGlobals` (32 bytes), `HectonStochasticSsrGlobals` (48 bytes), and `HectonVisorFluidDistortionGlobals` (128 bytes). Each uses `GraphicsBuffer.Target.Constant`, `LockBufferForWrite`, value-type DTOs, and `Shader.SetGlobalConstantBuffer`. HLSL shaders now consume `float4` lanes from named HECTON CBuffers. VR brownout and visor fluid now read player presentation state only through `GlobalRegistry.Player`. Retina MX350 selection now uses a change-only global keyword instead of material keyword mutation. The visor-fluid blackbox struct keeps explicit offsets but no longer declares `Pack=1`.
Rejected Alternatives: MaterialPropertyBlock was rejected because these are fullscreen global passes and MPB is not the requested ownership model. Real SSR was rejected in favor of the existing half-res R8 reflection sheen fake. Rewriting every remaining Visor renderer feature in one patch was rejected as compile-wall risk. Editing external AI/World compile errors was rejected as domain breach.
Scalability potential: Low/MX350 keeps fake-first effects with fewer material state writes and uses chromatic/half-res modes. Middle/High/Ultra retain the same ABI and can spend saved submission hygiene on stronger visor fluid, retina, and reflection polish without changing gameplay truth.
Hardware Impact: No profiler capture was run. Static removal: 6 dirty-frame material writes in VR brownout, 7 in retina distortion, 3 in stochastic SSR, and 24 in visor fluid distortion. CBuffer sizes are multiples of 16 and 8.

